From: h0cheung <hcheunh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Use the Python interpreter path provided by openSUSE

The upstream /bin/env shebang creates an unsatisfied RPM file dependency on
Tumbleweed, where env is provided at /usr/bin/env. Invoke Python directly.

--- a/usr/bin/steam-http-loader
+++ b/usr/bin/steam-http-loader
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-#!/bin/env python3
+#!/usr/bin/python3
 import urllib.parse
 import os.path
 import argparse
